# Echo Next.js Guidelines

## SDK Setup

### Server-Side Initialization
- Initialize the Echo SDK in a dedicated `src/echo/index.ts` file:
```typescript
import Echo from '@merit-systems/echo-next-sdk';

export const { handlers, isSignedIn, openai, anthropic } = Echo({
  appId: process.env.ECHO_APP_ID!,
});
```
- `ECHO_APP_ID` must be set in your `.env.local` file (server-side, no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ECHO_APP_ID` is used only in the client-side `EchoProvider`

### Client-Side Provider
- Wrap your app with `EchoProvider` in a client component:
```typescript
'use client';
import { EchoProvider } from '@merit-systems/echo-next-sdk/client';

export function Providers({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <EchoProvider config={{ appId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ECHO_APP_ID! }}>
      {children}
    </EchoProvider>
  );
}
```
- Always add `'use client'` directive to components using `EchoProvider` or `EchoTokens`

### API Route Handler
- Create a catch-all API route at `src/app/api/echo/[...echo]/route.ts`:
```typescript
import { handlers } from '@/echo';
export const { GET, POST } = handlers;
```
- This route handles Echo authentication and token management automatically

## AI Integration

### Using AI SDK with Echo
- Always import AI models from the Echo SDK, not directly from `@ai-sdk/openai`:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct — uses Echo billing
import { openai } from '@/echo';

// ❌ Wrong — bypasses Echo billing
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
```
- Use Vercel AI SDK v5 patterns for streaming:
```typescript
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@/echo';

const result = streamText({
  model: openai('gpt-4o'),
  messages,
});
```

### Auth Check
- Use `isSignedIn()` from `@/echo` to verify authentication in API routes before making AI calls

## Components

### EchoTokens
- Use `EchoTokens` component for the authentication/token purchase UI:
```typescript
'use client';
import { EchoTokens } from '@merit-systems/echo-next-sdk/client';
export function EchoButton() {
  return <EchoTokens />;
}
```
- Must be in a client component (`'use client'`)

## Environment Variables
- `ECHO_APP_ID` — Server-side Echo app identifier
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ECHO_APP_ID` — Client-side Echo app identifier (same value)
- Never commit `.env.local` to version control

## Project Structure
```
src/
  echo/
    index.ts          # Echo SDK init (server)
  providers.tsx       # EchoProvider wrapper (client)
  app/
    layout.tsx        # Root layout with Providers
    page.tsx          # App pages
    api/echo/[...echo]/
      route.ts        # Echo API handler
  components/
    EchoWrapper.tsx   # Client-side Echo components
```

## Common Patterns
- Always use Next.js 15 App Router (not Pages Router)
- Use `--turbopack` flag for dev server: `next dev --turbopack`
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 for styling
- Use `@/` path alias for imports from `src/`
